Subject: [PATCH] v8: turn write barriers back on

Qt's 6.11.2 tarball builds V8 with v8_disable_write_barriers = true on
every platform, which also turns on v8_enable_single_generation. V8 then
has no young generation. Every allocation goes to the old space, and the
collector can neither scavenge nor mark incrementally.

Qt restored Chromium's default on the 140-based branch of
qtwebengine-chromium in two changes by Allan Sandfeld Jensen, and
6.140.0 carries both. This is the two of them as one backport to
6.11.2. 770837 set the value to is_win, and 772657 set it to false.
The patch drops when the series moves to an engine that carries them.

On x86_64, JetStream 2.2 went from 0.718 to 0.917 of Chromium 140's
score and Speedometer 3.1 from 0.706 to 0.727 (omaweb#356).

